Day 10 – Bubble Sort (Started Coding)

Today I started writing the Bubble Sort code.

Before writing the complete algorithm, I tried to understand why Bubble Sort needs two loops. One loop is for one complete pass, and another loop is used to repeat the passes until the array becomes sorted.

I also understood why we use `range(len(arr)-1)` while comparing neighboring elements. Since we compare `arr[j]` with `arr[j+1]`, we cannot go to the last index because `j+1` would go outside the array.

