Q4--------------------------------------------------------

Why do we use `range(len(arr)-1)`?

Because we compare `arr[j]` with `arr[j+1]`. If we go until the last index, `j+1` will be outside the array.

Q5--------------------------------------------------------------

If an array has 6 elements, the worst case needs:

5 passes

My Code-----------------------------------------------

```python
arr = [3,2,1,0]
n = len(arr) - 1

for i in range(len(arr)):
    for j in range(n):
        if arr[i] > arr[j+1]:
            temp = arr[i]
            arr[i] = arr[j+1]
            arr[j+1] = arr[i]

print(arr)
```

